{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015qFsM1jY1Z3eTyXyhFeZYz","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ACL Rolling Review review form scoring scale overall assessment 2025 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review Data Collection (ARR-DC) - ARR Data Collection\",\"url\":\"https://arr-data.aclweb.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Dashboard\",\"url\":\"https://stats.aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ACL ARR 2025 May | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FMay\"},{\"title\":\"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing\"},{\"title\":\"Incentives 2026 – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \\\"Publish or Perish\\\" Circus | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the ACL Rolling Review form scoring scale and overall assessment:\n\n## Review Scoring Structure\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n## Soundness Score Requirements\n\nThe soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review. The excitement score is separate and more subjective, reflecting personal interest, which is orthogonal to the assessment of the soundness of the paper.\n\n## Conference Recommendation Standards\n\nAll papers recommended for Findings or main conference are expected to be sound and reproducible. A main conference paper could be distinguished by excitement, novelty, impact, and/or other factors, considered case-by-case.\n\nThe search results show information about the three-score system implemented in 2025, but specific numerical scale details (such as the exact point range for each score) were not fully detailed in these results. For more detailed scoring scale information, you may want to visit the official ACL Rolling Review review form page directly at aclrollingreview.org/reviewform.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72bdb13e-4703-43e0-b0b0-f41e588f3f9b","uuid":"324ec7ab-836c-4f2a-8b23-2d7e0df640e5","timestamp":"2026-05-15T12:29:42.977Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL Rolling Review review form scoring scale overall assessment 2025 2026","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01JRFM8if5eUnVhfLptCHwoZ","content":[{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review Data Collection (ARR-DC) - ARR Data Collection","url":"https://arr-data.aclweb.org/"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"ARR Dashboard","url":"https://stats.aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"ACL ARR 2025 May | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=aclweb.org%2FACL%2FARR%2F2025%2FMay"},{"title":"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing"},{"title":"Incentives 2026 – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2026"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \"Publish or Perish\" Circus | CSPaper Forum","url":"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about the ACL Rolling Review form scoring scale and overall assessment:\n\n## Review Scoring Structure\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n## Soundness Score Requirements\n\nThe soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review. The excitement score is separate and more subjective, reflecting personal interest, which is orthogonal to the assessment of the soundness of the paper.\n\n## Conference Recommendation Standards\n\nAll papers recommended for Findings or main conference are expected to be sound and reproducible. A main conference paper could be distinguished by excitement, novelty, impact, and/or other factors, considered case-by-case.\n\nThe search results show information about the three-score system implemented in 2025, but specific numerical scale details (such as the exact point range for each score) were not fully detailed in these results. For more detailed scoring scale information, you may want to visit the official ACL Rolling Review review form page directly at aclrollingreview.org/reviewform."],"durationSeconds":4.734518370999998}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014y8m4T1DjQ9vhrvDDwo8fE","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ARR review form overall assessment scale 1-5 soundness excitement\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Program Chairs’ Report on Peer Review at ACL 2023 Anna Rogers}\",\"url\":\"https://aclanthology.org/2023.acl-long.report.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"ACL’23 Peer Review Policies - ACL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/review-acl23/\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md\"},{\"title\":\"ACL’23 Peer Review Form - ACL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/review-form/\"},{\"title\":\"ACL 2023 Acceptance Recommendations - ACL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/overall-recommendation/\"},{\"title\":\"ACL 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/acl-statistics/acl-2025-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \\\"Publish or Perish\\\" Circus | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found detailed information about the ARR (ACL Rolling Review) form's overall assessment scale and its relationship to soundness and excitement.\n\n## ARR Review Scoring System\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n### Soundness Score (1-5 scale)\n\nThe soundness scale includes: 5 = Excellent (the study is one of the most thorough), 4 = Strong (provides sufficient support for all claims), and 3 = Acceptable (provides sufficient support for main claims). The soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review.\n\n### Excitement Score (1-5 scale)\n\nThe excitement scale includes: 5 = Highly Exciting (would recommend the paper to others and/or attend its presentation), 4 = Exciting (would mention the paper to others and/or make an effort to attend its presentation). Excitement scores reflect personal taste, and so do not necessarily come with explicit reasons.\n\n### Overall Assessment\n\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72bdb13e-4703-43e0-b0b0-f41e588f3f9b","uuid":"752e7fa8-90f2-4902-89f0-c202064e6877","timestamp":"2026-05-15T12:29:44.983Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ARR review form overall assessment scale 1-5 soundness excitement","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01StMuqPqZpjbjmxk9T1Yyrr","content":[{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"Program Chairs’ Report on Peer Review at ACL 2023 Anna Rogers}","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2023.acl-long.report.pdf"},{"title":"ACL’23 Peer Review Policies - ACL 2023","url":"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/review-acl23/"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md"},{"title":"ACL’23 Peer Review Form - ACL 2023","url":"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/review-form/"},{"title":"ACL 2023 Acceptance Recommendations - ACL 2023","url":"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/overall-recommendation/"},{"title":"ACL 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/acl-statistics/acl-2025-statistics/"},{"title":"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \"Publish or Perish\" Circus | CSPaper Forum","url":"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus"}]},"Based on the search results, I found detailed information about the ARR (ACL Rolling Review) form's overall assessment scale and its relationship to soundness and excitement.\n\n## ARR Review Scoring System\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n### Soundness Score (1-5 scale)\n\nThe soundness scale includes: 5 = Excellent (the study is one of the most thorough), 4 = Strong (provides sufficient support for all claims), and 3 = Acceptable (provides sufficient support for main claims). The soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review.\n\n### Excitement Score (1-5 scale)\n\nThe excitement scale includes: 5 = Highly Exciting (would recommend the paper to others and/or attend its presentation), 4 = Exciting (would mention the paper to others and/or make an effort to attend its presentation). Excitement scores reflect personal taste, and so do not necessarily come with explicit reasons.\n\n### Overall Assessment\n\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact."],"durationSeconds":6.4541070949999995}}
